/E (Online stores often list the same product using different names, descriptions, brands, and formats. Because of these variations, identifying whether two product listings represent the same real-world product becomes difficult. Traditional keyword-based searches may fail to recognize products with spelling differences, different word orders, abbreviations, or incomplete descriptions. This makes accurate product comparison and price analysis challenging. Therefore, there is a need for an efficient system that can identify, match, and group duplicate or similar product listings from different e-commerce sources using suitable Data Structures and Algorithms.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
